  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "Complete deep-bodied short-legged diprotodontid marsupial with conspicuously broad projecting cheek region. Not an isolated skull, actual rhinoceros or tapir. [\"Skin, coat, ears, tail and external soft-tissue contours inferred, not preserved.\", \"Mounted P17002 is incomplete, feet poorly visible and mount posture reconstructed. Do not treat every mount detail as fossil certainty.\", \"1859 paper contains obsolete synonymy and speculative horn/trunk assertions; use its actual cranium geometry/measurements only, not those conjectures.\", \"Historical plate fig5 is KOALA comparison, never use it as target nose.\"] {\"unit\": \"meter\", \"historical_cranium_length_m\": 0.4572, \"historical_zygomatic_width_m\": 0.381, \"measurement_basis\": \"Owen1859 p169 quotes Macleay original adult Sydney skull: approximately18in extreme length and15in widest zygoma. Historical approximate specimen dimensions, not direct measurement of P17002.\", \"head_body_length_m\": 2.1, \"shoulder_height_m\": 1.0, \"body_width_m\": 0.78, \"tail_length_m\": 0.18, \"whole_body_status\": \"Conservative illustrative living-body dimensions fitted to specimen skeletal proportions, NOT measured complete body. Official Naracoorte estimate300–500kg is contextual, not a geometry measurement.\"}",
    "zh": "原创低多边形研究；形态、尺度及不确定性严格以本次已核参考为界。原始限定：Complete deep-bodied short-legged diprotodontid marsupial with conspicuously broad projecting cheek region. Not an isolated skull, actual rhinoceros or tapir. [\"Skin, coat, ears, tail and external soft-tissue contours inferred, not preserved.\", \"Mounted P17002 is incomplete, feet poorly visible and mount posture reconstructed. Do not treat every mount detail as fossil certainty.\", \"1859 paper contains obsolete synonymy and speculative horn/trunk assertions; use its actual cranium geometry/measurements only, not those conjectures.\", \"Historical plate fig5 is KOALA comparison, never use it as target nose.\"] {\"unit\": \"meter\", \"historical_cranium_length_m\": 0.4572, \"historical_zygomatic_width_m\": 0.381, \"measurement_basis\": \"Owen1859 p169 quotes Macleay original adult Sydney skull: approximately18in extreme length and15in widest zygoma. Historical approximate specimen dimensions, not direct measurement of P17002.\", \"head_body_length_m\": 2.1, \"shoulder_height_m\": 1.0, \"body_width_m\": 0.78, \"tail_length_m\": 0.18, \"whole_body_status\": \"Conservative illustrative living-body dimensions fitted to specimen skeletal proportions, NOT measured complete body. Official Naracoorte estimate300–500kg is contextual, not a geometry measurement.\"}"
  },
